{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the setup logic and tests are sound. The one gap is incomplete `{impl}` marking of the `--path` option and its plumbing.\n\n**What the implementation does correctly**\n- In `src/setup.rs`, `run` reads `Cargo.toml` and calls `has_habeas_dev_dependency`. That function checks `[dev-dependencies].habeas`.\n- When no such dependency exists, `run` shells out to `cargo add --dev habeas --manifest-path <root>/Cargo.toml`. If `--path` was given, it appends `--path <canonicalized crate dir>`. The dependency is therefore a local-path dev dependency pointing at that crate.\n- When the dependency already exists, `run` skips `cargo add`. A repeated setup therefore adds no duplicate and leaves the manifest unchanged.\n- A failing `cargo add` returns an error. A missing crate directory also fails, because `fs::canonicalize` returns an error.\n- `has_habeas_dev_dependency` and the dependency-handling block in `run` are marked `{impl}` for `requirements.cli.setup_local_path`.\n\n**Tests**\n- Coverage is good. All of these are in `tests/setup.rs` and marked `{test}`:\n  - `local_path_setup_adds_exactly_that_crate_once` covers a relative `--path` resolved from the invocation directory. It checks exactly one `habeas` entry, in `dev-dependencies`, whose path resolves to the crate. It then repeats setup and checks the manifest is byte-identical.\n  - `local_path_setup_keeps_an_existing_habeas_dev_dependency` covers an existing dev dependency.\n  - `local_path_setup_rejects_a_missing_crate_directory` covers the failure case. It checks that setup fails and the manifest is untouched.\n  - `setup_is_repeatable` adds a double-run check of the same behavior.\n  - `habeas_dependencies` is the shared helper.\n\n**Gap: part of the implementation is not marked**\n- The `--path <crate-dir>` option is defined in `src/main.rs`, in the `Command::Setup { #[arg(long, value_name = \"crate-dir\")] path: Option<PathBuf> }` variant. That variant sits inside `enum Command`, which is marked `{impl}` only for `requirements.cli.clap`.\n- The match arm `Command::Setup { path } => setup::run(path.as_deref())` is marked `{impl}` only for `requirements.cli.setup`. It is the code that passes the option through to `run`.\n- Both pieces carry out part of this requirement: the `--path` trigger and its delivery to `run`. Neither has an `{impl}` reference to `requirements.cli.setup_local_path`. The instructions treat partially implementing code without an `{impl}` reference as a gap.\n- Fixing it needs only an `{impl}` marker on the `path` option and on the dispatch arm.\n\nNo FIXME acknowledges this gap, so the determination is false.",
